{
  "_comment": "Every category the app offers, in both modes and both languages. `id` is what the database stores and an API sends; `en` and `roman_ur` are only ever read by a human. Changing language changes the label and never the id, which is the whole point: a person's spending history cannot be reorganised by a settings toggle.",
  "_studentIdComment": "Student ids are the strings this app has stored since it began - 'Mess/Food', not 'food'. They read like English labels, and a clean-slate design would use slugs. Rewriting them would mean rewriting the category on every expense and budget row that already exists, and would buy nothing a person can see: an id that happens to be English is still an id, and it does not change when the language does. The householder ids added here are slugs, because nothing has been stored under them yet.",
